Round 28 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
  - `clang/runtime/eval_main.c`
- Implemented a strict-`MAT` DP fast path in head-mode emission:
  - `MAT` now probes scrutinees via `aot_try_mat_dp_ctr_match(...)` before generic `aot_force_strict(...)`.
  - On match (`DP0/DP1` over matching constructor), compiled code now:
    - skips full constructor duplication,
    - consumes the argument source exactly as before,
    - pushes lazy projected fields (`DP0`/`DP1` over original constructor fields) into `a_args`,
    - continues into the match branch.
- Extended probe helper to attempt one local WHNF force of DP payloads when payload tags are strict-forceable (`APP/ALO/REF/OP2/USE`) before deciding miss.
- Added opt-in probe telemetry (`HVM_AOT_MAT_DP=1`) and stderr dump line:
  - `AOT_MAT_DP probes/hits/non_dp/sub/non_ctr/ext_miss/force/force_to_ctr`.
- Wired telemetry dump in shared runtime eval path (`runtime_eval_main`).

Why this mattered
- `WNF_DUP_NOD` still dominates heap on heavy AOT benches. The goal was to bypass full `wnf_dup_nod` materialization in strict `MAT` when only branch routing + lazy fields are needed.
- Telemetry was needed to verify whether the new path is actually reached and why it misses.

